  "prefLabel": "Ahp 205.03 Waiver or Suspension of Rules by Presiding Officer",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ahp 205.03 Waiver or Suspension of Rules by Presiding Officer. The presiding officer, upon the motion of any party or intervenor, or on his or her own initiative, shall suspend or waive any requirement or limitation imposed by this chapter when the suspension or waiver:\n\n(a) Appears to be lawful; and\n\n(b) Is more likely to promote the just, accurate and efficient resolution of the pending dispute than would adherence to a particular rule or procedure.\n\nSource. #7232, eff 4-15-00; ss by #8078, eff 5-1-04",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ahp100-600.html"
